{
  "description": [
    "The accuracy set for estimating the position from the anchor (PLAN §3.2).",
    "",
    "Why it exists: in the webview the position is estimated without asking the",
    "core, so a second copy of the formula lives in JS. Two copies drift over time,",
    "and the drift starts where nobody notices — the progress bar lies by a few",
    "hundred milliseconds, nobody complains, and then in Phase 4 the same formula",
    "drives room sync.",
    "",
    "This file is the single source of truth both sides read. The Rust side:",
    "crates/headshell-core/tests/anchor_parity.rs. The JS side:",
    "crates/headshell/tests/anchor_parity_js.rs (running crates/headshell/ui/anchor.js in embedded QuickJS).",
    "",
    "Keys and case names are in English (D-036): this file is read from two",
    "languages, and whoever grows the set does not have to know anything else.",
    "",
    "wall_time and now are RFC 3339. expected_ms is an integer number of milliseconds."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "time advances while playing",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 10000,
        "rate": 1.0,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:05Z",
      "expected_ms": 15000
    },
    {
      "name": "paused does not advance",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 10000,
        "rate": 1.0,
        "state": "paused",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:05Z",
      "expected_ms": 10000
    },
    {
      "name": "buffering does not advance — no audio yet, so the counter must not run",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 10000,
        "rate": 1.0,
        "state": "buffering",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:05Z",
      "expected_ms": 10000
    },
    {
      "name": "stopped keeps the position where it is",
      "anchor": {
        "track": null,
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 0,
        "rate": 0.0,
        "state": "stopped",
        "duration_ms": null
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:05Z",
      "expected_ms": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "rate 0 does not advance even when the state says playing",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 10000,
        "rate": 0.0,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:05Z",
      "expected_ms": 10000
    },
    {
      "name": "phase 4 drift correction: rate 1.001 — TRUNCATED, not rounded",
      "note": [
        "100000 * 1.001 is not exactly 100100 in binary, it is 100099.999….",
        "The core truncates with `as u64`: 100099. If the JS side used Math.round",
        "it would say 100100 and the two copies would part ways here — the most",
        "valuable case in the set. The JS counterpart: Math.floor(elapsed_ms * rate)."
      ],
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 0,
        "rate": 1.001,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:01:40Z",
      "expected_ms": 100099
    },
    {
      "name": "a backwards clock jump does not rewind the position",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:10Z",
        "position_ms": 10000,
        "rate": 1.0,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
      "expected_ms": 10000
    },
    {
      "name": "does not exceed the duration",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 118000,
        "rate": 1.0,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": 120000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:30Z",
      "expected_ms": 120000
    },
    {
      "name": "no clamping when the duration is unknown",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 118000,
        "rate": 1.0,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": null
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:30Z",
      "expected_ms": 148000
    },
    {
      "name": "same instant: nothing has advanced",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 7321,
        "rate": 1.0,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
      "expected_ms": 7321
    },
    {
      "name": "sub-second: 1.5 s at rate 1.0",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00.000Z",
        "position_ms": 0,
        "rate": 1.0,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:01.500Z",
      "expected_ms": 1500
    },
    {
      "name": "half speed",
      "anchor": {
        "track": "mbid:1",
        "wall_time": "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
        "position_ms": 0,
        "rate": 0.5,
        "state": "playing",
        "duration_ms": 240000
      },
      "now": "2026-08-31T12:00:10Z",
      "expected_ms": 5000
    }
  ]
}
